# Repository-wide metadata: the citation covers both contracts and utilities.
# Version 0.1.0 is the forthcoming repository release, not the 1.1.2 generator.
# Preparing this file does not attest that the release has been published.
# Before tagging, add date-released with the actual release date (YYYY-MM-DD).
# Add a version-specific DOI only when one has actually been assigned.
# Do not add a guessed ORCID or a self-referential commit hash.
cff-version: "1.2.0"
message: >-
  When a study adopts these data-handling contracts or uses the accompanying
  utilities, please cite the repository release or full commit actually used.
  Identify the applicable contracts and document study-specific departures.
  Scholarly citation is requested for methodological traceability; it is not
  an additional condition of the MIT License. See docs/Citation and reuse.md.
type: software
title: "data-protocols: Data standard operating protocols"
authors:
  - family-names: "Costantini"
    given-names: "Carlo"
version: "0.1.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/costantinicarlo/data-protocols"
url: "https://github.com/costantinicarlo/data-protocols"
abstract: >-
  Scientific data-handling contracts and R utilities for reproducible data
  curation. The repository defines conventions for source-of-truth workbooks,
  key fields and identifiers, geographical coordinates, and toponym references.
  Accompanying tools retain source snapshots, assess observable compliance,
  extract original tables, produce derived coordinates, and resolve locality
  references using OpenStreetMap. Adopting a contract and executing a validator
  are distinct methodological activities.
keywords:
  - scientific data management
  - reproducibility
  - data provenance
  - data-handling protocols
  - workbook validation
  - geographical references
